{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevLwtrmMa2rFjfkT51Da","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All existing tests pass. Now I have a complete understanding of the repository structure.\n\n**Summary of Analysis:**\n\n- **Requirement:** Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking, atomic cancellation with all-or-nothing semantics when confirmed shipments exist, and shipment creation prevention on cancelled orders.\n\n- **Repository findings:** Order model (Order.kt:11-16) lacks status; OrderController (OrderController.kt:15-46) has create/read/list; OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27) provides in-memory storage; Shipment already has status field (Shipment.kt:9-14); ShipmentController and Repository follow same pattern; ApiExceptions hierarchy uses ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409); ErrorCode enum at ApiError.kt:31-37 has 5 codes; GlobalExceptionHandler at GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28 handles exceptions.\n\n- **Conventions:** Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError response `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`; Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap with save/findById/existsById/findAll/clear methods; Tests use @SpringBootTest/@AutoConfigureMockMvc with mockMvc and jsonPath assertions; Error codes follow [ENTITY]_[CONDITION] pattern.\n\n- **Affected files:** Order.kt (add OrderStatus and status field), OrderRepository.kt (add method to find by order id), OrderController.kt (add cancel endpoint), ShipmentRepository.kt (add findByOrderId method), ShipmentController.kt (add validation for cancelled orders), ApiError.kt (add error codes), OrderControllerTest.kt (add cancel tests), ShipmentControllerTest.kt (add cancelled order test).\n\n- **Risks:** Status field addition might affect serialization; concurrent access during cancel; all-or-nothing semantics with multiple shipments; idempotent cancellation logic.\n\n- **Open questions:** None—requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt:** Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to Order data class to track order lifecycle.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt:** Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to ShipmentRepository? No—inject ShipmentRepository into OrderController instead to avoid circular dependency.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt:** \n   - Inject `ShipmentRepository` \n   - Add new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` that:\n     - Finds the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return it immediately (idempotent)\n     - Find all shipments for this order\n     - If any shipment has status CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) with error code ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS (no changes to order or shipments)\n     - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED and update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n     - Persist the updated order and shipments\n     - Return the updated order\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt:** Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt:**\n   - Inject `OrderRepository` \n   - In the `create` method, after checking duplicate shipmentId, check if the order exists AND has status CANCELLED\n   - If order exists and is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409) with error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n   - If order doesn't exist, allow creation (keep current behavior)\n   - Otherwise proceed with normal creation\n\n6. **ApiError.kt:** Add two new error codes to ErrorCode enum:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - for when trying to create a shipment on a cancelled order\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` - for when trying to cancel an order that has confirmed shipments\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt:** Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Test cancelling an ACTIVE order moves it to CANCELLED and cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Test cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing (idempotent)\n   - Test cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing\n   - Test cancelling non-existent order fails with 404\n   - Test GET returns the order with correct status\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt:** Add tests:\n   - Test creating shipment for CANCELLED order fails with 409\n   - Test creating shipment for non-existent order still succeeds (backward compatible)\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- **Alternative:** Use a database/JPA instead of in-memory storage. **Rejected** because: requirement explicitly says \"no new dependencies\" and existing architecture is in-memory, so adding database dependencies would violate constraints.\n- **Alternative:** Make cancel endpoint idempotent by returning error on second cancel. **Rejected** because: requirement explicitly states \"Cancelling an order that is already CANCELLED succeeds and changes nothing. Customers retry this call, and a retry must not fail.\"\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order:**\n   - Controller receives POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns Order (ACTIVE)\n   - Find all shipments with orderId → filter to CREATED ones\n   - Check CONFIRMED shipments → none exist\n   - Set order.status = CANCELLED\n   - Update each CREATED shipment to CANCELLED status\n   - Repository.save(order)\n   - Response: 200 OK with updated Order\n\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED order:**\n   - Controller receives POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns Order (CANCELLED)\n   - Return the order as-is (idempotent)\n   - Response: 200 OK with Order (no change)\n\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Controller receives POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns Order (ACTIVE)\n   - Find all shipments → one has status CONFIRMED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, message)\n   - Nothing is saved\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - Controller receives POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, message)\n   - Response: 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope\n\n5. **Create shipment on CANCELLED order:**\n   - Controller receives POST /shipments\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns Order (CANCELLED)\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, message)\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n\n6. **Create shipment on non-existent order:**\n   - Controller receives POST /shipments\n   - Repository.findById(orderId) → returns null\n   - Proceed with creation (no validation of orderId)\n   - Response: 201 Created\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **OrderControllerTest.`cancel ACTIVE order`**: Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel, verify order is CANCELLED and shipment is CANCELLED\n- **OrderControllerTest.`cancel already CANCELLED order`**: Create order, cancel it, cancel again, verify second cancel succeeds and returns CANCELLED order\n- **OrderControllerTest.`cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment`**: Create order, create shipment, confirm it via direct repository write, attempt cancel, verify 409 and order/shipment unchanged\n- **OrderControllerTest.`cancel non-existent order`**: Attempt cancel, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- **OrderControllerTest.`GET returns status`**: Create order, verify status is ACTIVE; cancel order, verify status is CANCELLED\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.`cannot create shipment for CANCELLED order`**: Create and cancel order, attempt create shipment for it, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.`can create shipment for non-existent order`**: Attempt create shipment for non-existent order, verify 201 (backward compatible)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes as designed. Let me start:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2442,"cache_read_input_tokens":24242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2442},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07c853a4-60a1-4602-aafb-417a508c2e1a","uuid":"4d47ff8e-69b7-4b7d-bcc8-f182fd3991ea","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:54:31.497Z","request_id":"req_011CevLwtDozvWTqvTDuG9qN"}
